findings.body:
The PR blanks the English defaults for the add button and then leaves the stats-level text in an empty ternary, so the button renders only its icon.

::code{file="apps/stats/src/views/Stats/components/stats-filter.tsx" lines="496-505"}

`addButtonText={filters.length ? '' : ''}` always evaluates to `''`. In `Filters` the button renders `{addButtonText || mergedI18n.addFilter}`, and `addFilter` is now `''` in `DEFAULT_I18N`. The `title` (`addFilterTitle`) is also `''`. The result is a `<button>` with only an SVG icon and no `aria-label`, `title`, or text, which screen readers announce as an unlabelled button. Sighted users also lose the "Add filter" / "Filter" cue that was there before.

::callout{type="warning"}
The `DEFAULT_I18N` change is global to the shared `@tryghost/shade` filters component, so any other consumer that relies on the defaults gets the same regression.

If icon-only is the goal, keep an `aria-label` / `title` on the button. Otherwise, restore the labels and drop the dead ternary.

The PR adds `data-[state=closed]:!animation-none data-[state=closed]:!duration-0` to three popovers, apparently to suppress the close animation. The class `animation-none` does not exist in Tailwind 3.4 (the utility is `animate-none`), so Tailwind emits no CSS for it.

::diff{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="1201-1207"}

The base popover (`apps/shade/src/components/ui/popover.tsx`) applies `data-[state=closed]:animate-out` and `fade-out-0` / `zoom-out-95`. The `!duration-0` in this PR sets `transition-duration`, while `tailwindcss-animate` drives exit animations through `animation-duration`, so it does not cancel them either. The close animation most likely still runs on all three popovers (here, line ~1644, and the `Filters` popover around line 2081). The comment-free intent is unclear, so the fix should be verified in a browser.
